# Vinx Linux inittab (busybox init).
#
# ttyS0 is the person's console -- no login, straight to a root shell,
# because the "machine" is a tab they already own. ttyS3 is the control
# plane (rpcd's; see package/vinx-rpc); ttyS1 sits idle, reserved for the
# Phase 6 stream mux (the agentd that lived there retired in Phase 3, its
# job long since rund's via proc.run).
#
# devtmpfs is mounted first, before anything opens /dev/null or the serial
# nodes -- getty needs /dev/ttyS0 to exist. Guarded because some boot paths
# (v86's initramfs) mount it before init runs; the `[ -e /dev/null ]` probe
# keeps this idempotent and quiet instead of printing "mounting devtmpfs on
# /dev failed: Resource busy".

::sysinit:/bin/sh -c '[ -e /dev/null ] || /bin/mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev'
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /tmp
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /run
# The page's shared directory, a v86 9p filesystem: files dropped on the
# terminal land here, and the page snapshots it so it survives reloads.
# Guarded: a page that passes no `filesystem` option (or an old cached wasm)
# simply leaves /data an empty directory.
::sysinit:/bin/sh -c 'mkdir -p /data && mount -t 9p -o trans=virtio,version=9p2000.L host9p /data 2>/dev/null || true'
# /data/.vinx/tmp is the session-scoped resource namespace (system-v2
# §6.8): owners delete their own files, this sweep is the boot-time
# backstop for whatever an interrupted call stranded. (The .ble-*/.bridge-
# status polling files retired with the OSC protocol in Phase 3; the ble
# feed ring lives inside the swept namespace now.)
::sysinit:/bin/sh -c 'rm -rf /data/.vinx/tmp; mkdir -p /data/.vinx/tmp'
::sysinit:/bin/hostname -F /etc/hostname
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# -i: no /etc/issue -- the branding is /etc/profile.d/00-banner.sh, which can
# do colour and knows the machine's extra commands.
ttyS0::respawn:/sbin/getty -i -n -l /sbin/console-shell -L ttyS0 115200 vt100
# ttyS3 is the control plane. rpcd opens and configures the port itself
# (raw termios, TIOCEXCL, /run/vinx/rpcd.pid -- see package/vinx-rpc), so
# no tty is named here; rund serves proc.run over rpcd's Unix socket.
# Both exit on trouble and respawn clean (system-v2 §6.6).
::respawn:/usr/sbin/rpcd
::respawn:/usr/sbin/rund

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcK
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
